course: dictionary
lesson: 10824
title: Velcro: a brand name that became a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words start as the name of one company's product, and then people use that name for every product like it. Velcro is a brand name, so it begins with a capital letter, but people also say velcro for any hook-and-loop fastener.
explain: Context gives you clues. «Burrs are seed heads covered in tiny hooks» tells you that hooks are what let things stick. Velcro works the same way: one strip has tiny hooks and the other has tiny loops, so they cling together.
explain: Velcro can also be a verb in informal speech. To velcro something means to fasten it with Velcro. Check by swapping in your meaning: «He velcroed his trainers» means he fastened them with Velcro, and that makes sense.
fact: Velcro is a fastener made of two strips: one with tiny hooks and one with tiny loops.
fact: When you press the strips together they stick, and when you pull them apart they make a ripping sound.
fact: The Swiss engineer George de Mestral invented Velcro after looking at burrs stuck in his dog's fur.
fact: Burrs are seed heads covered in tiny hooks, which is why they cling to fur and clothes.
fact: Velcro is a brand name, but people use it for hook-and-loop fasteners in general, as in «Velcro shoes» and «Velcro strap».
exercise: «Burrs are seed heads covered in tiny hooks.» What are burrs covered in? | *Tiny hooks | Tiny loops | Sticky sap | Soft feathers
exercise: «Velcro shoes are easy for young children.» What does Velcro mean here? | A kind of shoelace | A brand of trainer | A rubber sole | *A fastener with hooks and loops
exercise: What happens when the two strips of Velcro are pressed together? | They melt | *They stick, and pull apart with a ripping sound | They stick together | They push apart
test: Velcro is made of two strips. One has tiny hooks. What does the other strip have? | Tiny wires | Tiny spikes | Tiny beads | *Tiny loops
test: Who invented Velcro after looking at burrs stuck in his dog's fur? | Marie Curie | Isaac Newton | Thomas Edison | *George de Mestral
exam: «He velcroed his trainers before the race.» What does velcroed mean? | To wash in a bucket | To tie with laces | *To fasten with Velcro | To paint in bright colours
